✅ Health check: {"status": "ok", "database": "connected", "version": "0.2.0"}
✅ DB save: Row inserted with id=1 to Neon PostgreSQL  
✅ DB query: 1 row found in predictions table
✅ Table auto-creation on startup: No errors
⚠️ /predict 500: OpenAI returned 429 (insufficient_quota) — API key issue, not code
```

## How It Works

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Client
    participant FastAPI
    participant OpenAI
    participant PostgreSQL

    Client->>FastAPI: POST /api/predict (MatchBundle)
    FastAPI->>OpenAI: GPT-4o mini (Structured Output)
    OpenAI-->>FastAPI: PredictionResponse JSON
    FastAPI->>PostgreSQL: Upsert prediction row
    PostgreSQL-->>FastAPI: Saved (match_id unique)
    FastAPI-->>Client: Return JSON response
```

## Next Step

Your OpenAI API key has hit its quota limit. Once refreshed or topped up, run:

```bash
python -m uvicorn app.main:app --port 8000
# Then test with:
python test_api.py
```
